ver get to  know it's stunning how much money was  sunk into this movie since despite all  of its name recognition it was never a  sure thing it's too dangerous but the  danger is what makes it fun  those are 2018 Robin Hood movie was  marketed with the tagline that the  legend do you know the story you don't  that's little more than wishful thinking  this story is extremely well known the  Robin Hood folktale has been told in  films literally dozens of times to the  point where even the most disengaged  person could rattle off the stories  basics Robin Hood has a green hat a bow  and arrow and a loyal CRO he Rob's from  the rich and gives to the poor there's a  friar named Chuck a maid named Marian  and a John who is little they're all  foxes you get the idea how does a studio  generate excitement for a story has been  done to death over 700 years it's a good  question and one this movie clearly  failed to crack Robin Hood's lukewarm  reception can partially be attributed to  a lack of interesting star power  director Otto Bathurst reportedly waited  a year for lead actor Taron Egerton to  become available for this reimagining  being determined to see him in the role  but why he explained his decision to the  corium male saying I wanted to find  someone who was accessible and who  seemed real and Taryn is like guy he is  incredibly charismatic and charming but  he also has serious intensity Terrance  got a really fantastic  everyman about him serving up the  emotional drama and then also fun  despite a relatively solid critical  track record  Edgerton has never proven himself to be  a huge draw in a lead role at least  outside of the success of the  star-studded Kingsman movies despite  technically being the protagonist of  that series edgerton's role has  generally been but one small part for  more famous ensemble even with a capable  assist from Jamie Foxx and others it's  possible that this cast just wasn't  enough of a draw for the well-worn  material if Robin 